  "summary": "Windows PE failure was an autodrop ownership/bootstrap problem, not an LLD PE link bug. The patch makes autodrop ownership conservative for borrowed-returning calls and handoff/reuse patterns, suppresses default autodrop when lowering the self-host compiler source, and pins current bootstrap semantics with #[manual_drop] markers so the checked-in old compiler can build a safe stage1."
